---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Motion
description: Aihio's motion durations and how they respond to reduced motion.
---
<section class="docs-page-intro">
  <p class="docs-page-intro__meta">Foundations</p>
  <h1>Motion</h1>
  <p>
    Motion is feedback, never decoration: a hover settles, a menu arrives. Every transition is timed from these tokens,
    and under <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code> they collapse to 1ms in one place, with no
    <code>!important</code> and nothing done to your own animation. Looping animation is switched off where it is
    declared instead, since a 1ms infinite rotation is a strobe. A build test fails if a component adds an animation
    without that guard.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="durations">
  <div class="docs-section-heading">
    <div>
      <h2>Durations</h2>
      <p>Point at a row to run its transition. With reduced motion on, they all jump, which is the point.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="docs-durations">
    {% for token in docs.foundations.duration.semantic %}
      <li class="docs-duration">
        <span class="docs-duration__track" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="docs-duration__dot" style="transition-duration: var({{ token.variable }})"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="docs-duration__text"><code>{{ token.variable }}</code> <span class="docs-muted">{{ token.value }}</span></span>
        <span class="docs-duration__description">{{ token.description | prose | safe }}</span>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h3 class="docs-api__heading">Scale</h3>
  <ul class="docs-link-row">
    {% for token in docs.foundations.duration.scale %}
      <li><code>{{ token.variable }}</code> <span class="docs-muted">{{ token.value }}</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
